Earpiece F-009: live VR knobs (overlay width, world scale) over PINE opcodes 0x30-0x32.
Applies on top of pcsx2-vr.patch (made against the pcsx2-vr tree as of 2026-11-03, which is
stock v2.6.3 + pcsx2-vr.patch). Compiled (PINE.cpp, VRSession.cpp) against that tree with MSVC;
not yet built into an executable or run in the headset: see earpiece RIG_CHECKLIST "F-009".

  cd pcsx2-vr; git apply ..r\pcsx2-knobs.patch     then rebuild as usual
  py vrr_knobs_selftest.py                         tests VRKnobs.h without PCSX2

What it adds (opcodes and ids from Earpiece decision 0005; the rig side is
earpiece-rig/src/earpiece_rig/pine.py and pcsx2_adapter.py):
- MsgVRKnobSet 0x30 (u8 id, f32 value -> nothing, clamped), MsgVRKnobGet 0x31 (u8 id -> f32),
  MsgVRKnobList 0x32 (-> u32 n, n x {u8 id, f32 lo, f32 hi, f32 value}). Unknown id or a
  non-finite value: IPC_FAIL. No VM needed (host memory).
- Knob 2 units_per_m (10..1000): OnEEVsync uses it for the eye offsets every vsync.
- Knob 5 flat_width_m (0.5..10): the flat-screen overlay is resized the next vsync it shows.
- Both seeded from [VR] UnitsPerMetre / FlatWidth; the ini is never written by the fork.

